The action list is read off the machine, not handed to the agent.

Every test here is written so that it FAILS on the version of this module that
needed a hand-written table of programs, flags, or subcommands. The claims:

  * a real GNU tool's own `--help` yields the operations it declares, with the
    numbers a reader can check against the tool;
  * a subcommand is admitted only when the program answers ABOUT it -- tar's
    prose words are refused, git's and ruff's real subcommands are admitted;
  * depth two is reached, because that is where a real tool keeps its options;
  * an operation that returns 0 and changes nothing is caught, and the tree is
    put back exactly;
  * an operation that only looks inert because the seed had the wrong FORM is
    recovered, and the form that worked is recorded;
  * a sorting tool pointed at a gzip stream is recorded as a binary rewrite, not
    as a success, because "changed" is not "did what you meant";
  * the census's own verdict becomes the action list `scan()` needs, and the
    scan then runs a real environment it was never told the actions for. a gnu tools own help yields the flags it documents a flag with aliases is one operation not three a tool with no subcommands admits none a program that ignores its argument does not admit a subcommand a real subcommand tree is admitted and walked depth two is where a tools own options live depth two reaches a modern tools real options a help text must declare something not merely mention an option a flag alone is not a door and the carrier makes it one a reader is judged on the artifact the machine just built a wrong seed form is not a no op until every form is tried a change is classified not merely counted an in place text rewrite is named as such and the tree is restored an operation that changed nothing is the answer worth having the census produces the action list the scan requires a door that moved nothing is never offered to the scan a clean exit that moves nothing is a sensor not a dead end a required operand makes an operation unbound rather than inert a required construction is supplied from the usage line a program that names no artifact is not given one a failed run that leaves a file is litter not a door the trials own seed write is never credited to the operation the tool reports every door with the kind of move it made

Tests for the history-induced edit grammar.

The rules that carry the round:

  * the grammar is INDUCED from real diffs and never written as an operator list in this file;
  * a task is real only if its test fails at the parent and passes at the commit -- otherwise it is refused;
  * a candidate is applied, judged, and the ORIGINAL BYTES ARE RESTORED even when the candidate breaks the
    file. A tree left modified would make every later measurement a lie;
  * the oracle (the commit's own edit) is EXECUTED, so "expressible" means "passes", not "fires";
  * "solved" is never inferred from a refusal state, and a refusal is always named. schema and zero model the grammar is induced from diffs and deduplicated a template fires only where its precondition holds sites inside the traceback function are searched first a candidate never leaves the tree modified a real failing test then a real passing fix the wrong source file is refused rather than guessed the oracle is executed so expressible means passes a traceback frame in the source is found and an assertion only failure is not summarise never counts a refusal as solved

Tests of the induced edit basis: where an edit comes from, and where it is allowed to act.

These tests are about the MECHANISM, so the programs in them are small and written here on purpose --
the corpus itself is the subject of `test_quixbugs_*.py` and of the receipt, not of a unit test.

What is pinned, in the order the claims matter:
  * a demonstration is folded into a template, and a template names its demonstrations;
  * an edit that changes the SHAPE of the code is refused, not approximated;
  * operator leaves are visible at all (the `^=` -> `&=` case, unreachable by the hand-listed basis);
  * a node-level demonstration generalizes to a hole pattern rather than to a literal string, and
    that pattern fires in a different program;
  * a template fires only where its precondition literally holds;
  * two sibling statements cannot be confused, because a site is identified by its path;
  * the rung a fix sits on is computed from the fix. operator pair on an augmented assignment is induced documentation is not a repair statement insertion is refused with a reason support counts distinct demonstrations refused templates never produce candidates a template fires in a different program and only at its precondition nothing fires where the old value is absent sibling statements are not confused a node edit generalizes to a hole not a literal a hole pattern fires in another program wrapping is expressed as containment repeated holes must bind equal subtrees a statement node edit is induced in statement mode an expression under a changed statement is preferred rungs are computed from the pairs a docstring only difference is no change at all

Pins what a single demonstration licenses, on a real repository, under different senses.

The laws these tests hold down, from `canonical/verification/ONE_DEMONSTRATION_BASIN_20261116_V1.json`:

  * the model is closed: 168 reachable states, 1680 real transitions, nothing truncated;
  * one demonstration of a real task has a domain strictly smaller than the environment, so "do it
    once" never covers the start states the environment actually offers;
  * under a status-level sense some states are undecidable: the demonstration fails where the agent
    perceives success, and no further demonstration can separate them;
  * reading ONE file removes only that file's share of the doubt, and reading every file removes all
    of it -- so the undecidable set is exactly the part of the goal the sense does not carry;
  * the shipped receipt is this run's numbers, not a memory of an older run. the model is closed and built from real transitions one demonstration covers less than the environment a status sense leaves a measured set undecidable reading one file removes only its own share of the doubt a sense that carries the premise licenses the whole domain the shipped receipt is this run

Tests for the renewability measurement.

Each rule here exists because it cost a measured error in this round:

  * a module that MOVES (packaging/ -> src/packaging/) is the same module -- keying by path made the
    biggest bump of the corpus report "nothing changed";
  * a module that does not import at the old revision taught nothing and is excluded, not counted as moved;
  * an arm that never RETURNED at the old revision was never learned -- a different exception at the new
    revision is not the environment moving a learned action (this inflated the moved set from 13 to 33);
  * a moved action must be split by KIND (removed / now raises / value changed), never added together;
  * blindness is per WITNESS as well as per prefix, because "learn it once" means one arbitrary witness. schema and zero model witnesses are deterministic and drawn from the module then the neutral tokens the split is a fixed rule not a seed the structural observable is the declaration not the behaviour a signature change is caught but must be classified by kind an action that never moves is stable a module that does not import at old is excluded not counted as moved an arm that never returned at old is not a learned action nondeterminism at the same revision is excluded and named kinds are never added together a module that move paths is the same module per witness risk is reported for every move headline reports every class apart

Tests for site identification by intervention.

The rules that must hold, because each one cost a measured failure:

  * the candidate set is NOT filtered by textual occurrence -- filtering by occurrence is the rule this
    module exists to replace;
  * a callable whose text contains the value but whose output ignores it is NOT the site;
  * a callable that needs the value as a COLLECTION is only sensitive in the element shape (this bug made
    the true `riscv64` site look inert);
  * the judge must re-encode the value in the shape the intervention discovered (this bug made a real
    discriminating pair read as wrong-at-fixed);
  * a responding site the change did not move is reported as such and never counted as a win. schema and zero model candidates are every callable not only the ones that mention the value counterfactuals come from the module s own vocabulary and end with the null occurrence is not sensitivity a collection is only reached in the element shape the judge honours the shape it was given a responding site the change did not move is not a win a real instruction names a discriminating site end to end nothing responds is refused by name every site responding is refused by name no direction and no value are refused before any execution headline reports every state apart

Tests for structural rewrite induction by anti-unification.

The rules that carry the round:

  * encode/decode must be a faithful round trip on real ASTs, or every downstream claim is noise;
  * generalisation must create a hole exactly where two subtrees disagree, and the same hole index must be
    re-usable in the replacement;
  * matching must bind a hole consistently (one hole, one subtree) or refuse;
  * a rule enters the grammar ONLY if it reproduces its own teaching diff -- the round-trip invariant;
  * a rewrite is installed at a POSITIONAL site, so a deepcopy cannot invalidate it (this round's first defect);
  * insert/delete diffs are named, not silently re-expressed as an update rule. encode decode is a faithful round trip generalisation puts a hole exactly where they disagree matching binds a hole consistently or refuses the round trip gate admits a faithful rule and rejects a lossy one a rewrite installs at a positional site and the source still parses insert delete is detected and named rather than modelled the encoding survives lists which ast requires summarise never counts a refusal or the baseline as a solve headline reports the baseline on the same sample single experience ast ir morphism transfers across repositories three way memory ablation on forty five unseen fixes multi statement subtree anti unification and o1 deletion verify boundary invariance 64 catches boundary crash and accepts safe patch federated self play distiller harvests and transfers multi statement skills

Pins what one demonstration can amortise in real engineering, from the shipped receipt.

The laws these tests hold down, from `canonical/verification/SYSTEMATIC_EDIT_SUPPLY_20261116_V1.json`:

  * the corpus is real history from five public repositories, pinned by sha256, so the numbers are
    reproducible offline and cannot drift silently;
  * only about a sixth of real commits contain a sibling site at all -- for the rest, "do it once"
    is one acquisition per instance, because there is nothing for the demonstration to generalise to;
  * where a sibling exists, most of what a demonstration gets right is a VERBATIM repeat: the same
    edit text belongs there too, so memory covers it and nothing has to be induced;
  * on the pairs that genuinely need induction, the demonstration reproduces the developer's edit
    about half the time and is wrong the other half -- which is the published ceiling, not perfection;
  * determinacy erodes with edit size: a five-line demonstration forces almost nothing. the corpus is real history and pinned only a minority of real commits have a sibling to learn from most of what memory covers is a verbatim repeat induction reproduces the developer about half the time determinacy erodes with edit size a stricter context rung shrinks supply and raises precision abstraction puts identifiers numbers and literals in holes induce rebinds what the target determines and flags what it cannot induce reports a value the demonstration cannot supply derivation carries the demonstrations own arithmetic onto the target a contrast only licenses the shift it can reproduce derived values are right only a fifth of the time on real history the derivation receipt is the run it claims to be
